0,Ternate language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ternate_language,"Ternate is a language of northern Maluku, eastern Indonesia. It is spoken by the Ternate people, who inhabit the island of Ternate, as well as many other areas of the archipelago. It is the dominant indigenous language of North Maluku, historically important as a regional lingua franca.",Ternate,West Papuan
